# ==========================================================

# Frontend Architecture Rules (Vue 3 + TS + Ionic)

# ==========================================================

Frontend structure under `/frontend`:

## Component + Styling Rules

- **Do NOT use Ionic UI components unless explicitly asked.**
- Default to **TailwindCSS + Flowbite** for UI components.
- Keep styling simple, utility-first, consistent.
- Use **vee-validate + zod** for frontend validation
- Use **vue-toastification** for notifications
- All errors must be handled gracefully by notifying the user
- Use interfaces instead of types

## Vue Rules

- Use `<script setup lang="ts">`.
- Use the Composition API exclusively.
- Use Pinia for global state.
- Create typed API clients under `frontend/src/lib/api`.
- No untyped JSON — define TS interfaces that match backend Spatie Data classes.
- Use component - composer - api structure
    - api file should contain the request, with specific return type
    - composer should contain any data and mainly error handling
    - component should only check if success flag is set
- for fetching data use "fetch" word in functions

## Routing

- Use lazy-loaded routes
- Add typed route params
- Protect routes with guard composables

## Capacitor (Android + iPhone)

- All device-specific APIs go under `/frontend/src/device/`
- Avoid DOM/browser-only APIs in core logic
- Keep the core of the app platform-agnostic

